<title>UK: IGC leaves 1997 wheat crop estimate unchanged.</title>
<headline>IGC leaves 1997 wheat crop estimate unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Grains Council on Thursday left its estimate for the 1997 world wheat crop at an unchanged 585 million tonnes.</p>
<p>This figure is four million tonnes higher than the already bumper 1996 crop, the IGC noted in its monthly Grains Market Report, issued on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Given normal growing conditions, production is expected to increase in the EU, Central/Eastern Europe, the former Soviet Union, the United States and India,&quot; the IGC said. --Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
